 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nString tokenization broken for escaped sequences and string boundaries\n\n#### Description\n\nString tokenization is producing incorrect results when processing strings with escape sequences and determining string boundaries. The tokenizer appears to be using incorrect operators when handling character sequences and string slicing.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom sqlglot.dialects import BigQuery\n\ntokenizer = BigQuery.Tokenizer()\n\n# This should tokenize correctly but produces wrong results\ntokens = tokenizer.tokenize(\"'{{ var('x') }}'\")\ntokens = [(token.token_type, token.text) for token in tokens]\nprint(\"Actual:\", tokens)\nprint(\"Expected: [(TokenType.STRING, '{{ var('), (TokenType.VAR, 'x'), (TokenType.STRING, ') }}')]\")\n\n# More complex jinja template also fails\nsql = \"\"\"\nSELECT\n   {{ x }},\n   {{- x -}},\n   {# it's a comment #}\n   {% for x in y -%}\n   a {{+ b }}\n   {% endfor %};\n\"\"\"\ntokens = tokenizer.tokenize(sql)\ntokens = [(token.token_type, token.text) for token in tokens]\nprint(\"Complex template tokens:\", tokens)\n```\n\nThe tokenizer is not correctly handling string boundaries and escape sequences, leading to malformed token parsing.\n</issue>\n",
